<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n95041" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκνίψ</span></b> , ὁ, gen.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκνῑπός</span>: nom. pl. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκνῖφες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Ex.</u>
					8.16(12)
				</span></i>
			, al., but 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκνῖπες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ps.</u>
					104(105).31
				</span></i>
			; acc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκνίπας [ῐ</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Ezek.
				<u>Exag.</u>
				135
			</span></i>:—an insect  found under the bark of
			trees, eaten by the woodpecker, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				614b1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Sens.</u>
				444b12
			</span></i> (in both places with 
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κνίψ</span>
			, which is the form used by <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.636d
			</span></i>: from its quick jump comes the prov., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ σκνὶψ ἐν χώρᾳ</span> '<i>a flea</i> at home!' <i><span class="en">
				Stratt.
				70
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Zen.
				5.35
			</span></i>:—an insect which attacks vines, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				12.186
			</span></i>. (Cf. Slav. <i>sknipa</i> 'gnat'.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
